@title Cooling what-if from the Cabinet Heat strip opens in 3D
@area Cabinet
@sizes 1366x768
# The button sits next to Cooling advice and Cooler layout in the Cabinet's Heat strip; the wizard previews in 3D, so the press takes the person there. A hotter day and a lighter duty are typed in the window before the run: the condition fields are there and the run is labelled a model.
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-cooling-advice.novo
wait 20
click_text Cabinet #1
wait 30
key ctrl+k
wait 6
text show or hide heat
wait 8
key Enter
wait 20
expect "Cooling what-if"
shot cabinet-heat-strip
check_layout
click_text "Cooling what-if"
wait 40
expect "Hottest day outside"
expect "MODEL, NOT MEASURED"
shot opened-in-3d
check_layout
